==================================
Packaging Uber Jars
==================================
[] For packaging a Uber Jar that you can use to run your app with java -jar app.jar, you have to add the following snipped to the end of your pom.xml.
This will essentially tell Maven what the main class is and that it should package all the dependencies into a single Uber Jar (using the Shade    
Plugin)

[] mvn3 package should trigger this and create app.jar under target. The non uber jar (w/o the dependencies) will be renamed under target as original-app.jar


  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
	<!-- Build an executable JAR -->
	<groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
	<artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
	<version>2.4</version>
	<configuration>
          <archive>
            <manifest>
              <addClasspath>true</addClasspath>
              <classpathPrefix>lib/</classpathPrefix>
              <mainClass>com.apple.analyzer.Parser</mainClass>
            </manifest>
          </archive>
	</configuration>
      </plugin>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-shade-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>2.3</version>
        <configuration>
          <!-- put your configurations here -->
        </configuration>
        <executions>
          <execution>
            <phase>package</phase>
            <goals>
              <goal>shade</goal>
            </goals>
          </execution>
        </executions>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>

